{% comment %}
  CartBloom app embed.

  An *embed* block (target: body), not an app block. Cart-drawer sections do not
  accept @app blocks, so the widget cannot be placed by the merchant there — it
  loads globally and mounts itself into the drawer. The cart *page* gets a real
  app block separately, where drag-and-drop placement does work.

  This file exists to do exactly one thing beyond loading assets: inline the
  offer config from the shop metafield. That is what keeps the storefront off
  our infrastructure entirely — no app proxy, no fetch, no latency, and no
  hosting cost that scales with a merchant's traffic (spec §4).

  If the metafield is missing or storefront access was never granted on its
  definition, `cfg` is nil and nothing renders. That is deliberate: a widget
  that renders a progress bar it cannot compute would show a wrong number.
{% endcomment %}

{% assign cfg = shop.metafields.app.cartbloom-widget-config.value %}

{% if cfg %}
  <script>
    window.__CARTBLOOM__ = {{ cfg | json }};
    window.__CARTBLOOM__.moneyFormat = {{ shop.money_format | json }};
    window.__CARTBLOOM__.routes = {
      cartAdd: {{ routes.cart_add_url | json }},
      cartChange: {{ routes.cart_change_url | json }},
      cart: {{ routes.cart_url | json }}
    };
  </script>

  {{ 'cartbloom.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}
  <script src="{{ 'cartbloom.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>
{% endif %}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "CartBloom progress bar",
  "target": "body",
  "settings": []
}
{% endschema %}
